# Local development on the microsandbox runtime. make up-microsandbox reads this
# after .env, so what is set here wins, and plain make up never reads it.
#
# The orchestrators run their tasks as microVMs in workload-microsandbox, the
# service compose.yaml starts under the microsandbox profile, instead of as
# containers on the docker service. That needs /dev/kvm: a Linux host, or the
# VM make lima-create makes on a Mac.
#
# The service's own certificate, WORKLOAD_MICROSANDBOX_CERT and
# WORKLOAD_MICROSANDBOX_KEY, sits in .env with the others: make certs issues it
# under the tunnel's authority and make certs-env prints it.
WORKLOAD_ORCHESTRATOR_RUNTIME=microsandbox

# Where the orchestrators reach the service, on the compose network. Its host is
# also where they reach the tasks' ports, which the service publishes.
WORKLOAD_MICROSANDBOX_URL=https://workload-microsandbox:8443
